Modern OpenGL

  We are going to use 

    - SDL to create a OpenGL Windows
    - GLAD that is a library that brings all the OpenGL functions to comunicate with the GPU.

Why do we us SDL2?

    SDL2:
        - Use this to render a windows to display an OpenGLContext
                                                ^~~~~~~~~~~~~ 
                        It is the large object that holds onto OpenGL.

                    The important thing it represent the frame buffers that rendering commands 

    - Handling I/O
    - Setupt subsytem: Sound/Networking/Images
    - Threading support


Setup:

1. SDL installation:

    $ sudo apt install libsdl2-dev       

2. GLAD:

  Go to GLAD: https://glad.dav1d.de/
  
  This is a tool library that allows us to query the OpenGL information in our setup

        Select options:

        Language: C/C++                               Specification: OpenGL
        API:                                          Profile: Core             
            * gl: Version 4.1
        Extensions
            ADD ALL
        
        Options:
            x Generate a loader

  Glad is a library which only declares functions in a header with no implementation. The actual implementation is in our
drver or OS.



